--- modules/cmdline/cmdline.man
+++ modules/cmdline/cmdline.man
@@ -155,10 +155,21 @@
 
 Starting with version 1.5 all errors thrown by the package have a
 proper [var ::errorCode] for use with Tcl's [cmd try] command. This
 code always has the word [const CMDLINE] as its first element.
 
+[para]
+
+The usage error thrown by [cmd ::cmdline::getoptions],
+[cmd ::cmdline::getKnownOptions] and [cmd ::cmdline::typedGetoptions]
+has the error code [const {CMDLINE USAGE}] when the help was explicitly
+requested via [option -?] or [option -help]. When the error is caused
+by an unknown option, a missing option argument, or an argument of the
+wrong type, the error code is [const {CMDLINE USAGE INVALID}] followed
+by a message describing the problem. A [cmd try] handler trapping
+[const {CMDLINE USAGE}] catches both.
+
